{"id":"cinnarizine","name":"Cinnarizine","form":"tablet","status":"Reference","source":"Wikidata","wikidata":"Q775073","aliases":"1-Benzhydryl-4-cinnamylpiperazin, 1-Cinnamyl-4-(diphenylmethyl)piperazine, Cinarizina, Cinnarizinum, R-1575, Stugeron®","category":"Other","chemicalClass":"","groups":[],"atc":["N07CA02"],"summary":"Cinnarizine is an antihistamine and calcium channel blocker of the diphenylmethylpiperazine group. It is prescribed for nausea and vomiting due to motion sickness or other sources such as chemotherapy, vertigo, or Ménière's disease. Cinnarizine is one of the leading causes of drug-induced parkinsonism.","summarySources":"Wikipedia","doseUnit":"","doseRows":[],"durationRows":[],"subjectiveEffects":[],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinnarizine"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on Cinnarizine","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q775073"},{"title":"PubChem","description":"Chemistry, safety and literature","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/1547484"}]}